{
  "schema": "whipplescript.model-limits.v1",
  "about": [
    "The largest prompt (input) and, for Claude, the output ceiling of each model the harness may",
    "drive. `input` is what the compaction trigger measures against: the catalog's max input where",
    "it states one, else its context window. `output` is the max_tokens the Anthropic wire sends",
    "when no budget was chosen, because that wire requires the field; an OpenAI-shaped wire is sent",
    "none (harness_model::model_output_limit), so other entries carry no `output`.",
    "",
    "An entry matches a model id that contains `match` with no letter or digit on either side of it,",
    "after any routing prefix up to the last `/`; the longest match wins. So a dated snapshot, a",
    "Bedrock or Vertex spelling and a metered-gateway name all resolve to their model's entry. A",
    "model no entry matches takes a fallback stated in harness_model.rs (WhippleScript DR-0161).",
    "",
    "`source: catalog` means model_catalog.json, the models.dev extract beside this file, and the",
    "kernel's tests hold every such entry to it: every model the extract lists has an entry of its",
    "own, a dated snapshot aside. Any other source is a provider page, read on the date in",
    "`checked`. `below` says why an entry deliberately states less than the catalog; `note`",
    "explains anything else. When the daily model-catalog job is red: run",
    "`node scripts/model-catalog.mjs --write`,",
    "then `cargo test -p whipplescript-kernel --lib model_limits`, and edit this file until that",
    "passes, checking each changed number against the provider's own model page."
  ],
